  "primary_subject_agency_ids": [],
  "summary": "Elgin Community College tried to cancel its Flock Safety contract in October 2025 and remove six campus cameras over fears about immigration enforcement affecting its largely Latino student body, but Flock refused and the cameras stayed until the contract expired in April 2026. The article situates Elgin's fight within a broader Illinois pattern of federal immigration access to Flock data at public colleges and growing pushback at other universities and cities nationwide.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "In October 2025, Elgin staff formally notified Flock that they wanted to cancel the contract and remove the equipment out of caution for students. Flock rejected the request within a day and refused to uninstall the cameras",
      "paragraph_idx": 6
    },
    {
      "quote": "Elgin staff began covering the cameras themselves, using black trash bags and zip ties \u2014 only to have workers in an unmarked vehicle repeatedly show up and strip the coverings away.",
      "paragraph_idx": 7
    },
    {
      "quote": "At the University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign and the University of Illinois Chicago, Flock data was searched dozens of times last year in connection with immigration enforcement.",
      "paragraph_idx": 11
    },
    {
      "quote": "outside law enforcement searched Flock data more than 650,000 times over a single 30-day period in July and August",
      "paragraph_idx": 15
    }
  ],
